WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:01.089
Good morning John!

00:00:01.089 --> 00:00:05.150
Last week I said some really mean things about
books, and books actually saw the video and

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:06.460
left a really nasty comment.

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:10.750
As an apology, let's talk about the best entertainment
investments you can make.

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:15.480
There are lots of different kinds and levels
of quality of entertainments, and also different

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:17.380
amounts of money you can spend being entertained.

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:20.110
Worst investments are usually live events.

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:22.730
Of course hopefully that means that the quality
of the entertainment is higher.

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:27.230
The Super Bowl, for example, this year a very
bad game, not interesting.

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:30.810
People pay upwards of two thousand dollars
to get a ticket to the Super Bowl for less

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:32.910
than four hours of entertainment!

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:36.640
That's, that's more than five hundred dollars
per hour of entertainment.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:38.870
That's about as bad as you can get.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:41.840
Vidcon- also a live event but it goes for
a long time.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:46.760
It's two days, and like, all the way around
almost, it's like 10 a.m. to 2 a.m.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:49.250
If you're spending all of that time being
entertained, and I hope you are, and you pay

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:53.460
the current 150 dollar per ticket price then
it's five dollars per hour of entertainment.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:54.460
That's pretty good!

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:58.399
It's the same as if you pay ten dollars for
a two-hour movie, as long as you don't buy

00:00:58.399 --> 00:01:00.570
the tremendously overpriced snack foods.

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:02.140
Also as long as you're not seeing a 3D movie.

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:06.280
Or in the special theater, or it's a special
edition movie, or you live in a place where

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:07.439
it's more than $10.

00:01:07.439 --> 00:01:11.749
Video games are one of the most popular forms
of entertainment these days, usually debuting

00:01:11.749 --> 00:01:14.710
about $60 and taking about 40 hours to beat.

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:15.729
Not bad at all!

00:01:15.729 --> 00:01:18.740
Comics, though I love them and they're beautiful
little pieces of art, and sometimes they do

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:20.999
hold on to their value- bad investment.

00:01:20.999 --> 00:01:24.799
Takes like 20 minutes to read and is 3 bucks,
so that's bad.

00:01:24.799 --> 00:01:28.060
Board games and card games are generally a
fantastic investment, so long as you play

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:29.060
them.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:31.740
So once you accept the cost, every time you
play it you are getting a better value.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:33.399
Now let's bring it on back to my friend books.

00:01:33.399 --> 00:01:37.090
The Fault in Our Stars is currently on sale
at Amazon for seven dollars.

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:39.200
This book, it took me about 20 hours to finish.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:42.419
I'm admittedly a slow reader so let's shave
some time off of that.

00:01:42.419 --> 00:01:44.009
46 cents per hour!

00:01:44.009 --> 00:01:45.389
This- now we're talking!

00:01:45.389 --> 00:01:50.869
At the same time though all of our other entertainments
are much more expensive than this, so really

00:01:50.869 --> 00:01:53.619
it's probably OK to pay full price for that
book.

00:01:53.619 --> 00:01:56.119
I'm only paying like 67 cents more per hour!

00:01:56.119 --> 00:02:00.020
Really, to me, that's the amount of money
I am paying to the local bookstore when I

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:03.039
buy it there rather than on Amazon.

00:02:03.039 --> 00:02:09.069
67 cents per hour of enjoyment that I am trading
in exchange for a place where I can go and

00:02:09.069 --> 00:02:10.530
look at books!

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.990
Nice people who will help me find things!

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:13.650
shelves and shelves of opportunity!

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:17.840
Of course, we haven't even mentioned America's
main source of

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:20.459
entertainment, that being television.

00:02:20.459 --> 00:02:24.170
Average cost of cable television package is
a hundred and twenty eight dollars per month.

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:27.430
Now that's a lot of money, but since the average
American spends -and I cannot believe this

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:33.099
is true- 34 hours per week watching television,
it's actually a really good deal!

00:02:33.099 --> 00:02:36.599
However, no one's pretending that the amount
of time you' spend watching TV is comparable

00:02:36.599 --> 00:02:38.819
to the amount of time you spend enjoying Vidcon.

00:02:38.819 --> 00:02:43.150
Hopefully, 20 hours of Vidcon is more than
10 times more entertaining than 20 hours of

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:44.150
television.

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:48.660
And yeah, I think 20 hours of reading a book
is probably more enriching than 20 hours of

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:49.720
playing Grand Theft Auto.

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:52.530
It doesn't seem like there's a huge amount
of correlation between the amount of dollars

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:55.720
delivered and the amount of value delivered,
which is why I guess it makes sense that a

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:57.210
lot of the best things in life are free.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.210
(singing Money (That's What I Want) by The
Beatles)

00:02:58.210 --> 00:03:00.799
But you can keep 'em for the birds and bees
I want money

00:03:00.799 --> 00:03:08.590
That's what I want
That's what I want

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:11.290
That's what I want

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:12.290
(speaking)

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:13.859
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

